---
title: New York Cheesecake
servings: 8
image: https://nonnafood.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/A-2-201.webp
---

== Crust ==

Combine @butter{1/4%cup}(softened), @graham crackers{1.75%cup}(crushed, about 1.5 wax packages), and @sugar{1/4%cup} in a #food processor{}.

Spread and press into a #10" glass pie pan{} until a crust forms.

Bake for ~{5%minutes} at 350*F, then set aside to cool.

== Filling ==

In a #bowl{}, whip @cream cheese{3%8zoz packages}(softened) and @vanilla{1%tsp}. Set aside.

In a #stand mixer{}, beat @egg whites{4} until stiff, starting at slow speed and working your way up.

Gradually add @sugar{2/3%cup}, beating constantly until sugar is dissolved.

Fold the cream cheese into the egg white/sugar combo.

Pour the filling into the cooled crust and spread evenly.

Bake for ~{30%minutes} at 375*F.

Let cool before consuming.

> The original recipe calls for 1 cup of sugar (total), but also 1/4 cup sugar and 2/3 sugar at each step. It's unclear where the error was, so we preserve the individual step amounts, even though it doesn't add up to 1 cup. Sometimes, the middle doesn't -quite- finish cooking. You might need to add another 10-15 minutes, maybe at 350*F just to be sure you don't burn things. Denise's BIL doesn't have this problem, we think he uses the full cup of sugar in the right ratio, so we should adjust at some point.